  "caveats": [
    "The comparison within a dataset is between DIFFERENT queries, not a paired one: queries containing a rare technical term may be harder for reasons other than tokenization. This bounds the channel; it does not isolate it.",
    "ArguAna and FiQA are on the teacher's disclosed training list; their gaps are deflated and they carry the caveat at the row.",
    "Word-level attribution counts a query once per DISTINCT fragmented word it contains, so a query with three of them contributes to three words.",
    "Excess is now measured against each word's OWN dataset's without-arm mean, so a hard dataset no longer inflates every word that appears in it."
  ]
}